27	/** The claims people on each sheet make. A claim left without a date is dated the sheet's entry date,
28	 * or its today when that is off. A claim's
29	 * terms are fixed when it is added, from those of its person's grade in force on its date, and its due-by
30	 * is the terms-th business day after that date, skipping weekends and the holidays on the sheet when it is added; the
31	 * claim belongs to the period containing that due-by (not its date). Only a DRAFT claim can be edited.
32	 * No claim whose due-by falls inside a closed period (not only soft-closed) can be added, edited or
33	 * change status, nor be edited to a date whose due-by, with its terms, would; one added with its due-by inside a soft-closed period is a late entry, and none can be added or edited to a date after its person's retirement date. A claim with a
34	 * negative amount is a correction: it is refused unless it names, by number, a SETTLED claim of the same
35	 * person; a claim that is not a correction names none. */
